// Example asus-user-status-led binding for Niri.
//
// This is a snippet, not a complete Niri configuration: insert the
// XF86Display line into the binds { } section of your existing config.
//
// Fn+1 arrives as XF86Display (verified on the ASUS ExpertBook B5402CBA)
// and cycles auto -> busy -> off -> auto. Niri repeats bindings while the
// key is held, so repeat=false keeps one press to exactly one cycle.
// The tilde is fine as is: Niri expands a leading ~ in the spawn program
// name.

XF86Display repeat=false { spawn "~/.local/bin/user-status-led" "cycle"; }
